            "result_text": "Done! The regex has been saved to `/app/regex.txt`. \n\nHere's how it works:\n\n- **`^(?=.*IPv4_pattern)`**: Ensures the line starts and contains a valid IPv4 address\n- **`.*?(?<![0-9a-zA-Z])(\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d))(?![0-9a-zA-Z])`**: Captures a date that isn't preceded/followed by alphanumerics\n- **`(?!.*date_pattern)`**: Negative lookahead ensuring this is the last date on the line\n\nWhen used with `re.findall(pattern, log_text, re.MULTILINE)`, it will:\n- Process each line independently\n- Skip lines without an IPv4 address\n- Extract only the last valid YYYY-MM-DD date from lines containing an IPv4\n- Avoid false matches like \"1134-12-12\" from \"user 1134-12-1234\""
